From: Christian Cortner <ccortner@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: CAPTURE size on S_FMT(OUTPUT), EOS only at end of drain, drain a resolution change before CAPTURE STREAMOFF

Three decoder fixes from one posted series (patches 3-5,
<20261028034335.26075-3-ccortner@gmail.com> .. -5-), carried as one:

1. Update the CAPTURE stride and size on S_FMT(OUTPUT). S_FMT on the
   OUTPUT queue updated the CAPTURE width and height but left
   bytesperline and sizeimage stale, so REQBUFS(CAPTURE) allocated
   buffers that buf_prepare then rejected with -EINVAL (seen at
   640x360). Hits clients that do not S_FMT(CAPTURE) again. Cc stable.
2. Signal V4L2_EVENT_EOS only at the end of a drain. EOS was queued, and
   the m2m context marked stopped, on every LAST buffer, the PSC_LAST of
   a source change included: a mid-stream resolution change emitted a
   spurious EOS (ffmpeg stops there), and the real end of stream none.
   Now gated on IRIS_INST_SUB_DRAIN_LAST. Cc stable.
3. Let a resolution change drain before stopping CAPTURE. ffmpeg's
   h264_v4l2m2m stops CAPTURE ~10 us after it dequeues a source change.
   If the stop reaches the firmware before the PSC_LAST buffer, that
   buffer still arrives, iris_inst_sub_state_change_drc_last() rejects
   it, and the instance goes to IRIS_INST_ERROR: no more buffers come
   back. iris_vb2_stop_streaming() now waits up to 500 ms for a pending
   source change to drain, and warns when it does not. On gen1 DRC_LAST
   is set when the event arrives, so the wait does not block there.

Fixes: 84e17adae3e3 ("media: iris: add support for dynamic resolution change")

Patch 2 of the series is the same change as our 1093. Taken from the
Steam Frame kernel's sm8650-7.2 branch (1b6de77b4, e36a8c68e, bac0a5707).
Bodies identical except iris_instance.h in (3): its include and the
drc_wq field are placed against this tree's context (1094's fields).
